{"subjectId":"javascript","id":"operators","title":"Operators","group":"Types, Values & Operators","order":11,"html":"<p class=\"lead\">Beyond arithmetic: short-circuit logic that returns operands, optional chaining, nullish coalescing, logical assignment and spread.</p>\n<section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-table\"></i>Operator families</h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Kind</th><th>Operators</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Arithmetic</td><td><code>+ - * / % **</code>, <code>++ --</code></td></tr><tr><td>Assignment</td><td><code>= += -= *= /= %= **=</code>, <code>&amp;&amp;= ||= ??=</code></td></tr><tr><td>Comparison</td><td><code>=== !== == != &lt; &gt; &lt;= &gt;=</code></td></tr><tr><td>Logical</td><td><code>&amp;&amp; || !</code>, <code>??</code></td></tr><tr><td>Bitwise</td><td><code>&amp; | ^ ~ &lt;&lt; &gt;&gt; &gt;&gt;&gt;</code></td></tr><tr><td>Other</td><td><code>?.</code>, <code>? :</code>, <code>typeof</code>, <code>instanceof</code>, <code>in</code>, <code>delete</code>, <code>void</code>, <code>,</code>, <code>...</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-arrows-split\"></i><code>&amp;&amp;</code> and <code>||</code> return an operand</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>console.log(\"a\" &amp;&amp; \"b\", 0 &amp;&amp; \"b\", \"a\" || \"b\", \"\" || \"b\");\nconsole.log(null || undefined || 0);\nconst user = { name: \"Kai\" };\nuser &amp;&amp; console.log(\"logged in as\", user.name);   // guard idiom</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>b 0 a b\n0\nlogged in as Kai</code></pre></figure>\n<p><code>a &amp;&amp; b</code> returns <code>a</code> if it is falsy, else <code>b</code>. <code>a || b</code> returns <code>a</code> if truthy, else <code>b</code>. Both <strong>short-circuit</strong>: the right side is not evaluated when unnecessary.</p>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-question-mark\"></i>Optional chaining <code>?.</code> and nullish coalescing <code>??</code></h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>const order = { customer: { address: null }, items: [], total() { return 42; } };\nconsole.log(order.customer?.address?.city);\nconsole.log(order.shipping?.method ?? \"standard\");\nconsole.log(order.items?.[0], order.total?.(), order.refund?.());\nconsole.log(order.customer.address?.city.toUpperCase());  // stops at null</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>undefined\nstandard\nundefined 42 undefined\nundefined</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"callout callout--warn\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Watch out</div><p><code>??</code> cannot be mixed with <code>||</code>/<code>&amp;&amp;</code> without parentheses: <code>a || b ?? c</code> is a SyntaxError. Write <code>(a || b) ?? c</code>.</p></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-equal\"></i>Logical assignment (ES2021)</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>const opts = { retries: 0, name: \"\", cache: null };\nopts.retries ||= 3;   // assigns if falsy\nopts.name &amp;&amp;= opts.name.trim();  // assigns if truthy\nopts.cache ??= new Map();        // assigns if null/undefined\nopts.timeout ??= 1000;\nconsole.log(opts);</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>{ retries: 3, name: '', cache: Map(0) {}, timeout: 1000 }</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-dots\"></i>Spread and rest <code>...</code></h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>const a = [1, 2], b = [3, 4];\nconsole.log([...a, ...b], Math.max(...b));\nconst base = { x: 1, y: 2 };\nconsole.log({ ...base, y: 20, z: 3 });\nfunction sum(...nums) { return nums.reduce((s, n) =&gt; s + n, 0); }\nconst [first, ...others] = [10, 20, 30];\nconsole.log(sum(1, 2, 3), first, others);</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>[ 1, 2, 3, 4 ] 4\n{ x: 1, y: 20, z: 3 }\n6 10 [ 20, 30 ]</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"callout callout--note\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Key point</div><p>Same syntax, opposite jobs: <strong>spread</strong> expands an iterable/object <em>into</em> places; <strong>rest</strong> collects remaining items <em>into</em> an array/object (parameters, destructuring).</p></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-plus-minus\"></i>Increment, exponent and a few odd ones</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>let i = 5;\nconsole.log(i++, i, ++i);\nconsole.log(2 ** 3 ** 2, (2 ** 3) ** 2);\nconsole.log(\"x\" in { x: undefined }, void 0, (1, 2, 3));\nconsole.log(5 &amp; 3, 5 | 3, 5 ^ 3, ~5, 1 &lt;&lt; 4, -16 &gt;&gt; 2, -16 &gt;&gt;&gt; 28);</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>5 6 7\n512 64\ntrue undefined 3\n1 7 6 -6 16 -4 15</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Precedence (high → low)</th><th>Examples</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Grouping, member, call</td><td><code>( )</code>, <code>.</code>, <code>?.</code>, <code>[]</code>, <code>f()</code>, <code>new</code></td></tr><tr><td>Postfix / prefix / unary</td><td><code>x++</code>, <code>!</code>, <code>typeof</code>, <code>-x</code></td></tr><tr><td>Exponent (right-assoc.)</td><td><code>**</code></td></tr><tr><td>Multiplicative → additive</td><td><code>* / %</code> then <code>+ -</code></td></tr><tr><td>Relational → equality</td><td><code>&lt; &gt; in instanceof</code> then <code>== ===</code></td></tr><tr><td>Logical</td><td><code>&amp;&amp;</code> then <code>||</code> then <code>??</code></td></tr><tr><td>Conditional, assignment, comma</td><td><code>? :</code>, <code>= += ??=</code>, <code>,</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<details class=\"qa\"><summary>What is the difference between || and ???</summary><div><p><code>||</code> returns the right side when the left is <em>falsy</em> (<code>0</code>, <code>''</code>, <code>false</code>, <code>NaN</code>, <code>null</code>, <code>undefined</code>). <code>??</code> only when the left is <code>null</code> or <code>undefined</code>, so valid values like <code>0</code> and <code>''</code> are kept.</p></div></details></section>"}